## 5. Testing Strategy

| Level | Scope | Tooling | When |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Unit** | Skill normalization, Skill Gap Engine status rules, Evidence Level computation, Priority formula, Readiness formula, roadmap DoD validation | Vitest | Written alongside each service in Phases 2, 4, 6, 8 |
| **Integration** | Every API route: request validation, auth/ownership enforcement, DB effects, error-path responses | Vitest + a disposable test Postgres schema/container | Written alongside each route group; consolidated pass in Phase 9 |
| **API/contract** | Response shapes match Architecture §8 exactly (`{ data }` / `{ error: { code, message } }`) | Same integration suite | Phase 9 |
| **Frontend** | Component-level rendering of loading/empty/error states for key widgets (`ReadinessGauge`, `RoadmapItemCard`, `SyncStatusIndicator`) | Vitest + React Testing Library | Phase 9–10 |
| **End-to-end** | PRD's three Core User Flows (A/B/C) run against a real (or preview) deployment | Playwright | Phase 9 |
| **AI evaluation** | Fixed job-description/resume fixtures checked for schema conformance and non-fabrication | Custom harness calling the real `AIProvider` | Phase 9, re-run on any prompt change |
| **Manual QA** | Accessibility keyboard pass, XSS-payload-in-text-field check, demo-scenario walkthrough | Human tester | Phase 10 |

**Non-negotiable coverage per Architecture's core decision:** every deterministic scoring/status function (Skill Gap Engine, Evidence Engine, Priority formula, Readiness formula) must have unit tests that pass **without any live AI or GitHub API call**, since these are explicitly designed to be explainable and reproducible independent of AI behavior.

