## 8. Git Strategy

- **Branches:** `main` (always deployable, protected, requires passing CI + 1 review); short-lived feature branches per task or small task group, named `phase-<n>/<short-description>` (e.g., `phase-4/target-crud`, `phase-6/skill-gap-engine`).
- **Commits:** Small, task-scoped commits referencing the phase/task number from this plan (e.g., `feat(phase-4): implement extractJobRequirements schema + prompt`). Avoid mixing schema migrations with unrelated feature code in the same commit.
- **Pull requests:** One PR per phase task (or a small cluster of closely related tasks); PR description references the Definition of Done checklist item(s) it satisfies; CI (lint, unit, integration) must pass before merge; every PR gets an automatic Vercel preview deployment for manual review.
- **Migrations:** Prisma migrations are committed with the PR that introduces the schema change; never edited after merging to `main` — a later change is a new migration.

